              "text": "armāmenta, armāmentōrum — \"a ship's tackle, the rigging; equipment\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Procella armāmenta nāvis frangit. The storm breaks the ship's rigging."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Second declension, neuter plural: armāmenta, armāmentōrum n. Masts, sails and ropes together. English armament comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "armāmenta is built on arma 'gear, equipment' (Lewis & Short) with the suffix -mentum. English armament comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
